Z||000019||Old Lar||07-31-2001||08:28 AM||||The whole concept of the two seater Fiero was that with the space age frame you could easily change body panels and get a new styled car.  You could update engines, suspensions (i.e. 88 suspension upgrade) and interiors with minimal development cost and have a new car.  When you see some of the rebodied cars, you can see the real potential for a long lived (limited production) car line.  As in todays market of the come back of the two seater "sports" car, GM/Pontiac was very sort sighted in killing off the Fiero line, but the upper management at GM has not been known to understand their customer base.||||reg||1
